than 80 tokens. Let me count... in Chinese the requirement is 80 tokens (which in English might be around 60 words).\n\nLet me think about this differently. With DeepSeek's caching, the system prompt is part of the cached prefix. Making it slightly longer doesn't add to the per-request cost if it's stable (it gets cached). The key is that it's STABLE and CONSISTENT.\n\nSo let me write a clear, concise system prompt that's maybe 100-150 tokens but stays exactly the same across requests. That way it always hits the cache for every subsequent request after the first.\n\nLet me write all the files now."}
