{"role":"assistant","content":"**不需要。** 这些 bug 都在 Flash 的能力范围内，原因如下：\n\n| 维度 | 评估 |\n|------|------|\n| **复杂度** | 全是 VS Code API 标准模式 + TypeScript/JS 常规修复，无需深度推理 |\n| **外部依赖** | 零——不涉及数据库、网络协议、第三方服务集成 |\n| **改动量** | 最大 20 行/文件，P0+P1 总共 ~50 行改动 |\n| **不确定性** | 每个 bug 的根因和修复路径都明确，没有需要探索的设计空间 |\n| **跨文件影响** | Bug 1+2 涉及 2 个文件联动，但逻辑简单清晰 |\n\n唯一相对需要小心的是 **Bug 2（语义令牌刷新）**——需要用 `EventEmitter` 模式让 `SemanticTokenProvider` 支持 `onDidChangeSemanticTokens`。但这个 API 用法在 VS Code 官方示例中很标准，我在 Flash 上完全可以处理。\n\n**结论：不需要 Pro。** 我现在开始按 P0 → P1 → P2 的顺序逐个修复？","reasoning_content":"The user is asking whether I think we need to escalate to DeepSeek Pro (the `<<<NEEDS_PRO>>>` mechanism) to fix these bugs, or if I can handle them on the current flash tier.\n\nLet me think about this:\n\n1. The bugs I found are all within the VS Code extension and bridge code I wrote\n2. They are straightforward TypeScript/JavaScript fixes\n3. None of them require complex architectural changes - they are isolated, well-understood bugs\n4. The fixes are small and clear (10-20 lines per bug)\n5. I don't need web search or external knowledge\n\nThe main bugs that need fixing:\n- Bug 1: Cross-module state sharing - simple refactor to use module-level variables\n- Bug 2: Semantic tokens refresh - add EventEmitter pattern (this is the trickiest one)\n- Bug 3: Hover switch - simple guard\n- Bug 4: Off-by-one - one character change\n- Bug 5: Response validation - add runtime check\n- Bug 6: Race condition - simple fix with abort controller or flag\n\nNone of these require Pro. They're all straightforward fixes that I can handle on the current model. The SemanticTokens refresh (Bug 2) is the most complex but still well within what Flash can handle - it's a standard VS Code API pattern.\n\nSo my answer: No, we don't need Pro. I can fix all of these on the current tier."}
