{"role":"assistant","content":"明白了——**只有打完一行（按 Enter）才触发分析**，行中编辑完全不触发。让我修正：","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_wfvoe45gQ5QMAD530h4V8299","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/AI   文件夹/mind-extension/src/extension.ts\", \"search\": \"/**\\n * 定时器（逐行分析 + 空闲防抖）\\n */\\nlet lineTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;\\nlet idleTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;\", \"replace\": \"/**\\n * 定时器（行完成分析）\\n * 只在按 Enter 后触发，行中编辑不触发任何分析\\n */\\nlet lineTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user is emphasizing:\n\n1. **Only analyze when a line is COMPLETE** (打完一行) - not on every Enter, but only after the ENTIRE line is fully written. This is what I already implemented with the `LINE_COMPLETE_DELAY` (200ms after Enter) and `MID_LINE_IDLE_DELAY` (2000ms idle). \n\nBut the user wants to emphasize this more strongly - only trigger analysis when the user finishes a complete line (hits Enter), not during mid-line editing.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"整个mind，只有一行写完才会开始分析和颜色改变以及提交给ai\" - the ENTIRE .mind file should only be analyzed when a line is COMPLETE. So:\n- Mid-line edits should NOT trigger analysis at all\n- Only pressing Enter (completing a line) should trigger analysis\n- The analysis then processes the ENTIRE file (all lines, to sync relationships)\n\nThis is different from what I implemented (I still had the 2000ms idle fallback). Let me adjust:\n- Mid-line editing: NO analysis triggered\n- Enter pressed: 200ms delay → analyze entire file\n\nLet me update the trigger logic to ONLY trigger on Enter, and remove the mid-line idle fallback completely.\n\nLet me also backup the current files first and then make the change."}
