{"role":"assistant","content":"通过。现在开始实现三文件体系。先备份当前状态，然后逐步实施。","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_Hx5OAtP6KrgKniHUy1m00862","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"powershell -Command \\\"$ts = Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd-HHmmss'; Copy-Item 'AI   文件夹/mind-extension/src/extension.ts' \\\\\\\"AI   文件夹/mind-extension/backups/extension.pre-triplet.$ts.ts\\\\\\\"; Copy-Item 'AI   文件夹/mind-extension/src/bridgeClient.ts' \\\\\\\"AI   文件夹/mind-extension/backups/bridgeClient.pre-triplet.$ts.ts\\\\\\\"; echo 'OK'\\\"\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Now let me start implementing the three-file system. Let me proceed with the plan steps.\n\nLet me start with Step 1 (bridge codeGenerator.js) and Step 2 (bridge /generate endpoint), then move to the plugin side.\n\nActually, I need to think about the `/generate` endpoint design more carefully before coding.\n\nThe `/generate` endpoint should:\n1. Receive the full .mind file content\n2. Extract lines that contain `# @d` (comments addressed to \"d老师\")\n3. Send to DeepSeek with a code generation prompt\n4. DeepSeek returns Python and C code implementations\n5. Parse the response into structured format with link mappings\n\nThe response should include position mappings:\n- For each `# @d` line in .mind → which function(s) in .py/.c implement it\n- The function's starting line in .py/.c\n\nLet me design the prompt for code generation:\n\n```\nYou are a code generation assistant. Given a .mind file with # @d comments (questions/requirements), generate both Python and C implementations.\n\nFor each # @d comment, create a function that fulfills the requirement.\n\nReturn in this exact JSON format:\n{\n  \"py\": {\n    \"code\": \"full Python file content with detailed comments\",\n    \"links\": [{\"mindLine\": 1, \"pyLine\": 10, \"name\": \"function_name\"}]\n  },\n  \"c\": {\n    \"code\": \"full C file content with detailed comments\",\n    \"links\": [{\"mindLine\": 1, \"cLine\": 12, \"name\": \"function_name\"}]\n  }\n}\n\nRequirements:\n- Python file must be valid, runnable Python 3 code\n- C file must be valid, compilable C11 code\n- Both files must have extensive Chinese+English comments explaining the code\n- Links connect the # @d comment line to the first line of the implementing function\n- If no # @d comments exist, return empty code with a note\n```\n\nActually, I realize I need to be more careful about the prompt format. Let me keep it concise.\n\nLet me now implement all the files. I'll start with the bridge side."}
