bat         ← 插件安装/打包脚本\n│   └── example.mind        ← 示例文件\n└── 示例文件/\n    └── demo.mind           ← 带 # @d 注释的完整示例\n```\n\nLet me create this. But I can't really \"copy\" files with the tools I have - I can write new files and use the existing ones. Let me think about the best approach.\n\nActually, the user probably wants me to organize the existing work into a clean package. Let me:\n\n1. Create the package folder structure\n2. Write the one-click startup script\n3. Write the installation guide\n\nFor the startup script, I need it to:\n- Check Node.js is installed\n- Install bridge dependencies\n- Start the bridge\n- Instruct user to install the VS Code extension\n- Create an example .mind file\n\nLet me also think about whether the user wants a separate \"package\" or just wants the existing folder structure improved. Looking at the current structure:\n\n```\nAI   文件夹/\n├── README.md\n├── 启动Mind系统.bat\n├── mind-bridge/\n├── mind-extension/\n└── resonix-agent/\n```\n\nI think the user wants a clean \"deliverable\" package that they can share or move around. Let me create a `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` folder with everything needed.\n\nActually wait - let me re-read: \"把相关的文件打包成一个文件夹\" - package the related files into ONE folder. So the current structure has mind-bridge and mind-extension as separate subdirectories of AI   文件夹. The user wants these packaged into a single folder.\n\nAnd: \"在文件夹里面加上一键傻瓜式引导启动装载文件\" - add a one-click foolproof guided startup file inside the folder.\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Create a clean package folder\n2. Copy the relevant files there (or create symlinks/references)\n3. Add a comprehensive one-click startup script\n\nSince I can't easily copy/move large directory trees with the available tools (write_file for individual files, move_file, copy_file for single files/dirs), let me use a different approach:\n\nI'll create the package folder with:\n1. The startup/install script (the main \"one-click\" file)\n2. Copy the key files into it\n3. Create batch/PowerShell scripts that handle everything\n\nActually, let me just create the package folder structure and write the startup script. The mind-bridge and mind-extension directories already exist - I can create a wrapper package.\n\nLet me create:\n```\nMind-语言系统/\n├── 一键安装启动.bat       ← Double-click this (main entry)\n├── 使用教程.txt           ← Step-by-step guide\n├── 示例.mind             ← Example .mind file with # @d\n├── mind-bridge/          ← Copy/link to existing\n│   └── ... \n└── mind-extension/       ← Copy/link to existing\n    └── ...\n```\n\nActually, copying large directories might be tricky. Let me create the startup script at the `AI   文件夹` level that references the existing directories, and create a proper \"package\" with scripts and documentation.\n\nLet me just create a `Mind-语言系统-安装包` folder with all the needed files. For the actual source code, I'll create symlinks or just reference the existing directories from the install script.\n\nLet me go with the simplest approach: Create a package folder with the startup script, documentation, and examples, while the actual code remains in mind-bridge/ and mind-extension/ directories. The startup script will handle everything from there."}
