{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_NvOZnBt5B1gqtB8k4C7s3261","type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/bridge/src\"}"}},{"id":"call_01_ZikcO669qYNB92hLcsRD0653","type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/extension/src\"}"}},{"id":"call_02_nf3lJJYVxrppnfc8yuQ71504","type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/extension/syntaxes\"}"}},{"id":"call_03_v9Qz5xYAtmQG2dJl1p0h6053","type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/package\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"OK, the `AI   文件夹` is inside the user's Desktop directory which is already a git repo (maybe initialized by the user or some other tool). The git status shows it's looking at the entire Desktop. That's not what we want.\n\nI should instead:\n1. Initialize a new git repo inside `Mind-语言系统-安装包` (or combine the two subdirectories into a single repo)\n2. Add the remote\n3. Commit and push\n\nActually, since mind-bridge and mind-extension are linked via junctions into the package folder, I should be careful about how git handles them. Junctions are treated as directories by git, not submodules.\n\nLet me create a proper git repo in the `Mind-语言系统-安装包` folder. But the junctions might cause issues with git since they're essentially symlinks.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully, the junctions point to directories in `AI   文件夹/mind-bridge/` and `AI   文件夹/mind-extension/`. Git on Windows handles junctions as regular directories, which means:\n- The junctions would be treated as the actual directories they point to\n- Git would try to track ALL files in mind-bridge (including node_modules)\n\nThat's not ideal. Let me take a different approach:\n\n1. Create a new git repo in a separate location\n2. Copy only the source files (not node_modules, dist, etc.)\n3. Add the remote\n4. Commit and push\n\nOr even simpler: create a `.gitignore` that ignores `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `backups/`, etc., and then init the repo in the `Mind-语言系统-安装包` folder.\n\nWait, but the junctions will point to the actual directories. If someone clones this repo on another machine, the junctions won't exist. The better approach is to make the `Structured-Pseudocode` repo contain the actual source code, not junctions to it.\n\nLet me create a proper repo structure:\n\n```\nStructured-Pseudocode/\n├── bridge/                  ← source from mind-bridge/src/\n├── extension/               ← source from mind-extension/src/ + syntaxes/ + configs\n├── package/\n│   ├── 一键安装启动.bat\n│   ├── 使用教程.txt\n│   └── 示例.mind\n├── .gitignore\n└── README.md\n```\n\nThis way the repo contains all the actual source files, not junctions.\n\nLet me create this in a temp directory structure and push it.\n\nActually, let me think about this more pragmatically. I'll:\n\n1. Create the repo directory\n2. Copy source files into it (excluding node_modules, dist, backups)\n3. Create .gitignore\n4. Initialize git\n5. Add remote\n6. Commit and push\n\nLet me do this step by step."}
