{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_Qb1mqvpfPBz0ShUFyiA91387","name":"read_file","content":"@echo off\nchcp 65001 >nul\ntitle Mind 语言系统 — 一键安装启动\ncd /d \"%~dp0\"\n\n:: ============================================================\n:: Mind 语言系统 — 一键傻瓜式安装启动器\n:: ============================================================\n:: 功能:\n::   1. 检查系统环境（Node.js、npm、VS Code）\n::   2. 安装桥接服务依赖\n::   3. 构建 VS Code 插件\n::   4. 启动桥接服务\n::   5. 提示安装插件\n::   6. 创建示例文件\n:: ============================================================\n\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\n\n:MENU\ncls\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║                                                      ║\necho ║       🧠 Mind 自然语言语义标注系统                    ║\necho ║       ─────────────────────────────                   ║\necho ║       一键安装 · 启动 · 管理                         ║\necho ║                                                      ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\necho 请选择操作:\necho.\necho   [1] 🚀 一键安装 + 启动（推荐）\necho   [2] 🔧 仅安装（不启动服务）\necho   [3] ▶  仅启动桥接服务\necho   [4] 📦 打包 VS Code 插件\necho   [5] ❓ 查看使用教程\necho   [0] 退出\necho.\nset /p choice=\"请输入数字 (0-5): \"\n\nif \"%choice%\"==\"1\" goto INSTALL_AND_START\nif \"%choice%\"==\"2\" goto INSTALL_ONLY\nif \"%choice%\"==\"3\" goto START_ONLY\nif \"%choice%\"==\"4\" goto PACKAGE\nif \"%choice%\"==\"5\" goto TUTORIAL\nif \"%choice%\"==\"0\" exit /b\ngoto MENU\n\n:INSTALL_AND_START\ncls\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║  步骤 1/5: 检查系统环境                              ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\n\n:: 检查 Node.js\nwhere node >nul 2>&1\nif %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n    echo [✗] Node.js 未安装！\n    echo     请从 https://nodejs.org/ 下载安装 Node.js 18+\n    echo     安装后重新运行此脚本\n    pause\n    exit /b\n)\nfor /f \"tokens=2\" %%v in ('node --version 2^>nul') do set NODE_VER=%%v\necho [✓] Node.js: %NODE_VER%\n\n:: 检查 npm\nwhere npm >nul 2>&1\nif %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n    echo [✗] npm 未安装！\n    pause\n    exit /b\n)\nfor /f \"tokens=1\" %%v in ('npm --version 2^>nul') do set NPM_VER=%%v\necho [✓] npm: %NPM_VER%\n\n:: 检查 VS Code\nwhere code >nul 2>&1\nif %errorlevel% equ 0 (\n    echo [✓] VS Code: 已安装\n) else (\n    echo [!] VS Code 命令行工具未找到\n    echo     不影响桥接服务，但需要 VS Code 来安装插件\n)\n\necho.\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║  步骤 2/5: 安装桥接服务依赖                          ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\necho 正在安装 mind-bridge 依赖...\n\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"\nif not exist \"package.json\" (\n    echo [✗] 未找到 mind-bridge 目录！\n    echo     请确保脚本在正确的位置运行\n    pause\n    exit /b\n)\n\ncall npm install\nif %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n    echo [✗] 依赖安装失败！\n    pause\n    exit /b\n)\necho [✓] 桥接服务依赖安装完成\n\necho.\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║  步骤 3/5: 构建 VS Code 插件                         ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\necho 正在构建 mind-extension...\n\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-extension\"\nif not exist \"package.json\" (\n    echo [✗] 未找到 mind-extension 目录！\n    pause\n    exit /b\n)\n\ncall npm install\ncall npm run build\nif %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n    echo [✗] 插件构建失败！\n    pause\n    exit /b\n)\necho [✓] 插件构建成功\n\necho.\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║  步骤 4/5: 启动桥接服务                               ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\necho 正在启动 Mind Bridge (端口 3456)...\necho 提示: 首次启动需要连接 DeepSeek API，需等待 20-30 秒\necho.\n\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"\nstart \"Mind Bridge\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"\n\n:: 等待服务启动\necho 等待服务就绪...\ntimeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul\n\n:: 检查是否启动成功\ncurl -s http://localhost:3456/health >nul 2>&1\nif %errorlevel% equ 0 (\n    echo [✓] 桥接服务启动成功！(端口 3456)\n) else (\n    echo [!] 桥接服务可能还在启动中...\n    echo     请稍后访问 http://localhost:3456/health 检查\n    echo     或在任务管理器中检查是否有 node.exe 进程\n)\n\necho.\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║  步骤 5/5: 安装 VS Code 插件                         ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\necho 两种方式安装插件:\necho.\necho  方式 A — 从 VSIX 安装（推荐）:\necho     1. 打开命令行 → cd \"%~dp0mind-extension\"\necho     2. 运行: npx vsce package\necho     3. 在 VS Code 中: 扩展 → ... → 从 VSIX 安装\necho.\necho  方式 B — 开发模式:\necho     1. VS Code 打开 \"%~dp0mind-extension\"\necho     2. 按 F5 启动扩展开发模式\necho     3. 新窗口中打开 .mind 文件\necho.\necho  方式 C — 直接复制文件夹:\necho     将 mind-extension 文件夹复制到\necho     %%USERPROFILE%%\\.vscode\\extensions\\ 目录\necho.\necho ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\necho  🎉 安装完成！\necho  现在你可以在 VS Code 中创建 .mind 文件了\necho  示例文件: \"%~dp0示例.mind\"\necho ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\necho.\n\npause\ngoto MENU\n\n:INSTALL_ONLY\ncls\necho [安装] 仅安装依赖，不启动服务...\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"\ncall npm install\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-extension\"\ncall npm install\ncall npm run build\necho [✓] 安装完成\npause\ngoto MENU\n\n:START_ONLY\ncls\necho [启动] 启动桥接服务...\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"\nstart \"Mind Bridge\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"\ntimeout /t 3 /nobreak >nul\ncurl -s http://localhost:3456/health >nul 2>&1\nif %errorlevel% equ 0 (\n    echo [✓] 桥接服务已在运行 (端口 3456)\n) else (\n    echo [!] 服务可能还在启动，请稍后检查\n)\npause\ngoto MENU\n\n:PACKAGE\ncls\necho [打包] 生成 VS Code 插件安装包 (.vsix)...\ncd /d \"%~dp0mind-extension\"\ncall npx vsce package\nif %errorlevel% equ 0 (\n    echo [✓] 插件打包成功！\n    dir /b *.vsix 2>nul\n) else (\n    echo [!] 打包失败，请检查错误信息\n)\npause\ngoto MENU\n\n:TUTORIAL\ncls\necho ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\necho ║              Mind 语言系统 — 使用教程                 ║\necho ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\necho.\necho  ─── 第一步: 启动桥接服务 ───\necho  运行本脚本 → 选 [1] 一键安装启动\necho  或手动: cd mind-bridge ^&^& npm start\necho.\necho  ─── 第二步: 安装 VS Code 插件 ───\necho  方式 A: cd mind-extension ^&^& npx vsce package\necho         然后安装生成的 .vsix 文件\necho  方式 B: 用 VS Code 打开 mind-extension 文件夹\necho         按 F5 启动开发模式\necho.\necho  ─── 第三步: 创建 .mind 文件 ───\necho  新建文件，后缀 .mind，例如 test.mind\necho.\necho  ─── 第四步: 写需求，自动生成代码 ───\necho  在 .mind 中用 # @d 开头写需求:\necho.\necho    # @d 实现链表反转\necho    # 要求: 输入头节点，返回反转后的头\necho    Define function reverse_list\necho    if head is null return null\necho.\necho  写完按 Enter → 自动分析 → 生成同目录下:\necho    test.py   (Python 实现，含详细注释)\necho    test.c    (C 实现，含详细注释)\necho.\necho  ─── 第五步: 超链接导航 ───\necho  在 .mind 中点击 # @d 注释 → 跳转到 .py/.c 函数\necho  在 .py/.c 中点击函数注释 → 跳回 .mind 需求\necho.\necho  ─── 快捷键 ───\necho  Ctrl+Shift+P → \"Mind: 立即分析\"\necho  Ctrl+Shift+P → \"Mind: 显示状态\"\necho.\necho  ─── 设置 ───\necho  VS Code 设置 → 扩展 → Mind Language\necho  (颜色/缩进线/端口/行为 全部可调)\necho.\npause\ngoto MENU"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_PyJyIl5Vp5UzAmo07Wn81767","type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/package/一键安装启动.bat\", \"range\": \"91-110\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Let me analyze the batch file for bugs:\n\n1. **`for /f \"tokens=2\" %%v in ('node --version 2^>nul')`** — `node --version` outputs something like `v24.15.0`. With `tokens=2`, it will not capture anything meaningful because there's only one token (the version string). This will result in `NODE_VER` being empty. Should use `tokens=*` or just capture the whole line.\n\n2. **Same issue with npm** — `npm --version` outputs `11.12.1`, `tokens=1` would work but having `2^>nul` with the caret escaping might cause issues. Actually `2^>nul` in a FOR loop is correct for supressing stderr.\n\n3. **`curl` might not be available on all Windows systems** — On older Windows (pre-10 or pre-1803), curl is not built-in. Should have a fallback.\n\n4. **The `start` command** — `start \"Mind Bridge\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"` — this starts a new cmd window, but the `cd` to mind-bridge directory happens before the `start` command. However, `start` creates a NEW cmd process that inherits the current working directory... actually, does it? In Windows, `start` with a title `\"Mind Bridge\"` as the first quoted argument uses that as the window title, and the next argument `cmd` is the command. The `/c` runs the command and terminates. But the `&& pause` is part of the cmd command string. This should work, but the `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"` from before `start` sets the CWD for the CURRENT batch process, not the new cmd window. The new cmd window would inherit the CWD from the parent process.\n\nWait, actually `start` does inherit the current directory. So if we did `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"` first, then `start \"...\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"`, the new cmd window would start in the mind-bridge directory. This should be fine.\n\nBut there's a subtle issue: if `%~dp0` expands to a path with the `AI   文件夹` (with multiple spaces), the `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"` uses quotes so it should handle spaces correctly.\n\n5. **`%NODE_VER%` might be empty** — the `for /f` parsing of `node --version` output.\n\n6. **`for /f \"tokens=1\" %%v in ('npm --version 2^>nul')`** — `npm --version` outputs `11.12.1`. With `tokens=1`, it captures `11.12.1` correctly. The `2^>nul` is correct for suppressing stderr in a FOR loop.\n\nBut wait, there's a known issue: `node --version` outputs to stderr or stdout? On most Node.js installations, `node --version` outputs to stdout. The `2^>nul` only suppresses stderr, so this should be fine.\n\n7. **Missing `chcp` output suppression** — `chcp 65001 >nul` changes the code page to UTF-8, which is good for Unicode characters. But this might cause issues if the console font doesn't support the box-drawing characters.\n\n8. **The `choice` command alternatives** — The script uses `set /p` for input, which works. But if the user enters nothing, `choice` is empty, and the script falls through to `goto MENU`.\n\n9. **`dir /b *.vsix 2>nul`** — In the PACKAGE section, this lists .vsix files. But after `npx vsce package`, the output might show the filename. This is fine.\n\n10. **`timeout /t 5 /nobreak`** — `/nobreak` prevents the user from skipping the timeout. This is fine.\n\n11. **Missing error handling when `cd /d` fails** — If the mind-bridge or mind-extension directory doesn't exist, the script should fail gracefully. The `if not exist \"package.json\"` check handles this, but only after `cd`.\n\n12. **The `%NODE_VER%` and `%NPM_VER%` variables** — They're set inside the `setlocal enabledelayedexpansion` block. But they're used with `%NODE_VER%` which is standard expansion, not `!NODE_VER!`. In a batch file, `%var%` expansion happens when the line is parsed, not when it's executed. In a FOR loop, the entire block is parsed at once, so `%NODE_VER%` inside the loop might not capture the value correctly.\n\nWait, but the FOR loop is not inside a parenthesized block in this case. Let me look again:\n\n```\nfor /f \"tokens=2\" %%v in ('node --version 2^>nul') do set NODE_VER=%%v\necho [✓] Node.js: %NODE_VER%\n```\n\nThis is at the top level (not inside an IF block), so `%NODE_VER%` expands after the FOR loop completes. This should be fine.\n\nBut there's another issue: `node --version` on Windows typically outputs `v24.15.0` (with the `v` prefix). With `tokens=2`, the FOR loop splits on spaces and tabs. Since there's only one token, `tokens=2` won't capture anything. Should use `tokens=*` or just leave it as `tokens=1`.\n\n13. **`npx vsce package`** — This command installs and runs `vsce`. But `vsce` was installed globally earlier. However, in a fresh environment without global vsce, `npx vsce package` should work.\n\nActually, wait - I think the major bugs are:\n\n1. **`for /f \"tokens=2\" %%v in ('node --version')` is wrong** — should be `tokens=1` or just capture the full line.\n\n2. **`npm --version` with `tokens=1`** — This correctly captures the version number.\n\n3. **The bat is in the `package/` directory in the git repo, but the junctions are in `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` in the user's AI文件夹.** The actual paths the bat uses depend on where it's placed relative to mind-bridge and mind-extension.\n\nLet me look at the specific bugs:\n\n### Bug 1: `node --version` parsing\n`node --version` outputs `v24.15.0` (single token). Using `tokens=2` means it splits on delimiters (space/tab) and takes the second token. Since there's only one token (no spaces), `tokens=2` captures nothing. `NODE_VER` remains empty.\n\nFix: Change to `tokens=1` or just use the full line.\n\nActually, let me test this:\n```\nC:\\> node --version\nv24.15.0\n```\n\nSo `for /f \"tokens=2\" %%v in ('node --version') do set NODE_VER=%%v` would set `NODE_VER` to empty because there's only one token (the entire output).\n\nThe fix: Use `\"tokens=1\"` or better, just capture the whole thing.\n\n### Bug 2: `npm --version` also uses `2^>nul`\n`tokens=1` captures the version correctly. This should work.\n\n### Bug 3: `curl` might not be installed\nOn Windows, `curl.exe` is included starting from Windows 10 version 1803. Since the user is on Windows, it's likely available, but not guaranteed.\n\n### Bug 4: The `start` command might not preserve the working directory\nWhen using `start \"title\" cmd /c \"command\"`, the new cmd window starts in the current directory of the batch process. But actually, on Windows, `start` by default uses the CWD of the parent process. So the `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"` before `start` should set the CWD for the new window.\n\nBut wait - there's a subtle issue: after `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"`, if we then `start \"Mind Bridge\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"`, the `node src/index.js` path is relative to the CWD, which is now the mind-bridge directory. This should work.\n\n### Bug 5: `timeout` output\nThe `timeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul` redirects to nul, which suppresses the \"Waiting for X seconds, press a key to continue...\" message. This is correct.\n\n### Bug 6: `curl` check for health\n`curl -s http://localhost:3456/health >nul 2>&1` — the `>nul` redirects stdout, `2>&1` redirects stderr to stdout (which is also redirected to nul). This should silently check the health endpoint.\n\nBut if `curl` is not installed, this will show \"curl is not recognized...\" and `errorlevel` will be non-zero, which leads to the \"[!] 桥接服务可能还在启动中...\" message. This is actually graceful degradation.\n\n### Bug 7: `set /p` input validation\nIf the user just presses Enter without typing anything, `choice` is empty. The script then goes to `:MENU` (after the `if` checks fail). This is correct behavior, but not very user-friendly.\n\n### Bug 8: `%NODE_VER%` and `%NPM_VER%` unused after display\nThey're only used for display. Not a bug, just unused.\n\n### Bug 9: The actual critical bug - the `/generate` endpoint isn't mentioned in the startup banner\nThis was already fixed in the bridge but the package startup script might show old information. Let me check... The script says \"POST /analyze — 分析 .mind 文件\" but doesn't mention `/generate`. Actually, the startup banner is in the bridge code, not the batch file. The batch file just starts the bridge.\n\nWait, looking at the bridge's index.js, we already updated the banner to include `/generate`. So the bridge startup banner is correct.\n\n### Bug 10: Unicode display issues\nThe batch file uses Unicode characters like `🧠`, `├─`, `└─`, `│`, `╔═╗`, `✅`, `❌`, `👍`, etc. On Windows, the default console code page (437 or 936) doesn't support these characters. The `chcp 65001` changes to UTF-8 code page, which helps, but the console font needs to support these glyphs.\n\nOn Windows 10+ with the default terminal (Windows Terminal or new console host), this usually works. On older Windows, these characters will show as `?` or boxes.\n\n### Bug 11: `exit /b` in the main menu\nWhen the user selects [0], `exit /b` exits the batch script. But `setlocal enabledelayedexpansion` is active, and `exit /b` will end the script. This is correct.\n\nLet me now list the specific bugs I found:\n\n1. **`tokens=2` in node --version parsing** → `NODE_VER` will be empty\n2. **No curl fallback** → if curl isn't available, health check silently fails\n3. **No errorlevel check after `cd /d`** → if directory doesn't exist, subsequent `if not exist` check fails\n4. **Console Unicode rendering** → For maximum compatibility, should avoid Unicode box-drawing characters or add a note about font requirements\n\nLet me fix these bugs."}
