{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_cQrEWY097f7MzKF3i1IR8546","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"powershell -Command @\\\"\\n$lines = @(\\n'@echo off',\\n'chcp 65001 >nul 2>&1',\\n'title Mind Language System',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0\\\"',\\n'setlocal enabledelayedexpansion',\\n'',\\n':MENU',\\n'cls',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  ===== Mind Language System =====',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo         1. Install + Start (recommended)',\\n'echo         2. Install only',\\n'echo         3. Start bridge only',\\n'echo         4. Package VS Code extension',\\n'echo         5. Usage tutorial',\\n'echo         0. Exit',\\n'echo.',\\n'set /p choice=\\\"Enter number (0-5): \\\"',\\n'',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"\\\" goto MENU',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"1\\\" goto INSTALL_AND_START',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"2\\\" goto INSTALL_ONLY',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"3\\\" goto START_ONLY',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"4\\\" goto PACKAGE',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"5\\\" goto TUTORIAL',\\n'if \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"0\\\" exit /b',\\n'goto MENU',\\n'',\\n':INSTALL_AND_START',\\n'cls',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo ==== Step 1/5: Check Environment ====',\\n'echo.',\\n'',\\n'where node >nul 2>&1',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\\n'    echo [X] Node.js not found!',\\n'    echo     Download from https://nodejs.org/',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'for /f \\\"delims=\\\" %%v in (''node --version 2^>nul'') do set NODE_VER=%%v',\\n'echo [OK] Node.js: %%NODE_VER%%',\\n'',\\n'where npm >nul 2>&1',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\\n'    echo [X] npm not found!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'for /f \\\"delims=\\\" %%v in (''npm --version 2^>nul'') do set NPM_VER=%%v',\\n'echo [OK] npm: %%NPM_VER%%',\\n'',\\n'where code >nul 2>&1',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\\n'    echo [OK] VS Code: installed',\\n') else (',\\n'    echo [!] VS Code CLI not found (OK, only needed for extension)',\\n')',\\n'',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo ==== Step 2/5: Install Bridge Dependencies ====',\\n'echo.',\\n'',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\" 2>nul',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\\n'    echo [X] mind-bridge directory not found!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'if not exist \\\"package.json\\\" (',\\n'    echo [X] package.json not found!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'call npm install',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\\n'    echo [X] npm install failed!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'echo [OK] Bridge dependencies installed',\\n'',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo ==== Step 3/5: Build VS Code Extension ====',\\n'echo.',\\n'',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" 2>nul',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\\n'    echo [X] mind-extension directory not found!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'if not exist \\\"package.json\\\" (',\\n'    echo [X] package.json not found!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'call npm install',\\n'call npm run build',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\\n'    echo [X] Build failed!',\\n'    pause',\\n'    exit /b',\\n')',\\n'echo [OK] Extension built',\\n'',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo ==== Step 4/5: Start Bridge Service ====',\\n'echo.',\\n'',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\"',\\n'start \\\"Mind Bridge\\\" cmd /c \\\"node src/index.js && pause\\\"',\\n'echo Waiting for service...',\\n'timeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul',\\n'',\\n'call :CHECK_HEALTH',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\\n'    echo [OK] Bridge running on port 3456',\\n') else (',\\n'    echo [!] Bridge may still be starting...',\\n'    echo     Check http://localhost:3456/health',\\n')',\\n'',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo ==== Step 5/5: Install VS Code Extension ====',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Option A -- Install from VSIX:',\\n'echo     cd \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\"',\\n'echo     npx vsce package',\\n'echo     VS Code: Extensions -^> ... -^> Install from VSIX',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Option B -- Developer mode:',\\n'echo     Open \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" in VS Code',\\n'echo     Press F5',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  ========================================',\\n'echo    All done! Create a .mind file to start',\\n'echo  ========================================',\\n'echo.',\\n'pause',\\n'goto MENU',\\n'',\\n':INSTALL_ONLY',\\n'cls',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\" 2>nul && call npm install',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" 2>nul && call npm install && call npm run build',\\n'echo [OK] Done',\\n'pause',\\n'goto MENU',\\n'',\\n':START_ONLY',\\n'cls',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\" 2>nul',\\n'start \\\"Mind Bridge\\\" cmd /c \\\"node src/index.js && pause\\\"',\\n'timeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul',\\n'call :CHECK_HEALTH',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\\n'    echo [OK] Bridge running on port 3456',\\n') else (',\\n'    echo [!] Bridge may still be starting',\\n')',\\n'pause',\\n'goto MENU',\\n'',\\n':PACKAGE',\\n'cls',\\n'cd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" 2>nul',\\n'call npx vsce package',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\\n'    echo [OK] Extension packaged!',\\n'    dir /b *.vsix 2>nul',\\n') else (',\\n'    echo [!] Package failed',\\n')',\\n'pause',\\n'goto MENU',\\n'',\\n':TUTORIAL',\\n'cls',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  ============ Mind Language System ============',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Step 1: Start bridge service',\\n'echo    Run this script -^> option [1]',\\n'echo    Or: cd mind-bridge ^&^& npm start',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Step 2: Install VS Code extension',\\n'echo    cd mind-extension ^&^& npx vsce package',\\n'echo    Install .vsix in VS Code',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Step 3: Create .mind file, write requirements',\\n'echo    Use # @d prefix for code generation:',\\n'echo      # @d reverse linked list',\\n'echo      Define function reverse_list',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Step 4: Press Enter -^> auto analyze -^> generates:',\\n'echo    test.py  (Python with comments)',\\n'echo    test.c   (C with comments)',\\n'echo.',\\n'echo  Step 5: Click # @d comment to jump to code',\\n'echo.',\\n'pause',\\n'goto MENU',\\n'',\\n':CHECK_HEALTH',\\n'where curl >nul 2>&1',\\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\\n'    curl -s http://localhost:3456/health >nul 2>&1',\\n'    exit /b %%errorlevel%%',\\n')',\\n'powershell -Command \\\"try { $r = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri ''http://localhost:3456/health'' -TimeoutSec 3; exit 0 } catch { exit 1 }\\\" >nul 2>&1',\\n'exit /b %%errorlevel%%'\\n)\\n\\n$content = ($lines -join \\\"`r`n\\\") + \\\"`r`n\\\"\\n[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText('Structured-Pseudocode/package/一键安装启动.bat', $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::Default)\\nWrite-Host \\\"File written: $($content.Length) bytes\\\"\\n\\\"@\", \"timeoutSec\": 10}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Let me use PowerShell to create the batch file with proper ANSI encoding and CRLF line endings."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_cQrEWY097f7MzKF3i1IR8546","name":"run_command","content":"$ powershell -Command @\"\n$lines = @(\n'@echo off',\n'chcp 65001 >nul 2>&1',\n'title Mind Language System',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0\"',\n'setlocal enabledelayedexpansion',\n'',\n':MENU',\n'cls',\n'echo.',\n'echo  ===== Mind Language System =====',\n'echo.',\n'echo         1. Install + Start (recommended)',\n'echo         2. Install only',\n'echo         3. Start bridge only',\n'echo         4. Package VS Code extension',\n'echo         5. Usage tutorial',\n'echo         0. Exit',\n'echo.',\n'set /p choice=\"Enter number (0-5): \"',\n'',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"\" goto MENU',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"1\" goto INSTALL_AND_START',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"2\" goto INSTALL_ONLY',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"3\" goto START_ONLY',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"4\" goto PACKAGE',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"5\" goto TUTORIAL',\n'if \"%%choice%%\"==\"0\" exit /b',\n'goto MENU',\n'',\n':INSTALL_AND_START',\n'cls',\n'echo.',\n'echo ==== Step 1/5: Check Environment ====',\n'echo.',\n'',\n'where node >nul 2>&1',\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\n'    echo [X] Node.js not found!',\n'    echo     Download from https://nodejs.org/',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'for /f \"delims=\" %%v in (''node --version 2^>nul'') do set NODE_VER=%%v',\n'echo [OK] Node.js: %%NODE_VER%%',\n'',\n'where npm >nul 2>&1',\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\n'    echo [X] npm not found!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'for /f \"delims=\" %%v in (''npm --version 2^>nul'') do set NPM_VER=%%v',\n'echo [OK] npm: %%NPM_VER%%',\n'',\n'where code >nul 2>&1',\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\n'    echo [OK] VS Code: installed',\n') else (',\n'    echo [!] VS Code CLI not found (OK, only needed for extension)',\n')',\n'',\n'echo.',\n'echo ==== Step 2/5: Install Bridge Dependencies ====',\n'echo.',\n'',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\" 2>nul',\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\n'    echo [X] mind-bridge directory not found!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'if not exist \"package.json\" (',\n'    echo [X] package.json not found!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'call npm install',\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\n'    echo [X] npm install failed!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'echo [OK] Bridge dependencies installed',\n'',\n'echo.',\n'echo ==== Step 3/5: Build VS Code Extension ====',\n'echo.',\n'',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-extension\" 2>nul',\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\n'    echo [X] mind-extension directory not found!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'if not exist \"package.json\" (',\n'    echo [X] package.json not found!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'call npm install',\n'call npm run build',\n'if %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (',\n'    echo [X] Build failed!',\n'    pause',\n'    exit /b',\n')',\n'echo [OK] Extension built',\n'',\n'echo.',\n'echo ==== Step 4/5: Start Bridge Service ====',\n'echo.',\n'',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"',\n'start \"Mind Bridge\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"',\n'echo Waiting for service...',\n'timeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul',\n'',\n'call :CHECK_HEALTH',\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\n'    echo [OK] Bridge running on port 3456',\n') else (',\n'    echo [!] Bridge may still be starting...',\n'    echo     Check http://localhost:3456/health',\n')',\n'',\n'echo.',\n'echo ==== Step 5/5: Install VS Code Extension ====',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Option A -- Install from VSIX:',\n'echo     cd \"%~dp0mind-extension\"',\n'echo     npx vsce package',\n'echo     VS Code: Extensions -^> ... -^> Install from VSIX',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Option B -- Developer mode:',\n'echo     Open \"%~dp0mind-extension\" in VS Code',\n'echo     Press F5',\n'echo.',\n'echo  ========================================',\n'echo    All done! Create a .mind file to start',\n'echo  ========================================',\n'echo.',\n'pause',\n'goto MENU',\n'',\n':INSTALL_ONLY',\n'cls',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\" 2>nul && call npm install',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-extension\" 2>nul && call npm install && call npm run build',\n'echo [OK] Done',\n'pause',\n'goto MENU',\n'',\n':START_ONLY',\n'cls',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\" 2>nul',\n'start \"Mind Bridge\" cmd /c \"node src/index.js && pause\"',\n'timeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul',\n'call :CHECK_HEALTH',\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\n'    echo [OK] Bridge running on port 3456',\n') else (',\n'    echo [!] Bridge may still be starting',\n')',\n'pause',\n'goto MENU',\n'',\n':PACKAGE',\n'cls',\n'cd /d \"%~dp0mind-extension\" 2>nul',\n'call npx vsce package',\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\n'    echo [OK] Extension packaged!',\n'    dir /b *.vsix 2>nul',\n') else (',\n'    echo [!] Package failed',\n')',\n'pause',\n'goto MENU',\n'',\n':TUTORIAL',\n'cls',\n'echo.',\n'echo  ============ Mind Language System ============',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Step 1: Start bridge service',\n'echo    Run this script -^> option [1]',\n'echo    Or: cd mind-bridge ^&^& npm start',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Step 2: Install VS Code extension',\n'echo    cd mind-extension ^&^& npx vsce package',\n'echo    Install .vsix in VS Code',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Step 3: Create .mind file, write requirements',\n'echo    Use # @d prefix for code generation:',\n'echo      # @d reverse linked list',\n'echo      Define function reverse_list',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Step 4: Press Enter -^> auto analyze -^> generates:',\n'echo    test.py  (Python with comments)',\n'echo    test.c   (C with comments)',\n'echo.',\n'echo  Step 5: Click # @d comment to jump to code',\n'echo.',\n'pause',\n'goto MENU',\n'',\n':CHECK_HEALTH',\n'where curl >nul 2>&1',\n'if %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (',\n'    curl -s http://localhost:3456/health >nul 2>&1',\n'    exit /b %%errorlevel%%',\n')',\n'powershell -Command \"try { $r = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri ''http://localhost:3456/health'' -TimeoutSec 3; exit 0 } catch { exit 1 }\" >nul 2>&1',\n'exit /b %%errorlevel%%'\n)\n\n$content = ($lines -join \"`r`n\") + \"`r`n\"\n[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText('Structured-Pseudocode/package/一键安装启动.bat', $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::Default)\nWrite-Host \"File written: $($content.Length) bytes\"\n\"@\n[exit 1]\n所在位置 行:1 字符: 101\r\n+ ... m.Text.Encoding]::UTF8;$OutputEncoding=[System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8;@\r\n+                                                                         ~\r\n源文本中包含无法识别的标记。\r\n所在位置 行:116 字符: 1\r\n+ 'start Mind Bridge cmd /c node src/index.js\r\n+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n字符串缺少终止符: '。\r\n所在位置 行:116 字符: 45\r\n+ 'start Mind Bridge cmd /c node src/index.js\r\n+                                             ~\r\n子表达式中缺少右“)”。\r\n    + CategoryInfo          : ParserError: (:) [], ParentContainsErrorRecordException\r\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : UnrecognizedToken\r\n \r\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_JDOtvLyGEm0px76t3TAo3994","type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"content\": \"$batContent = @\\\"\\n@echo off\\nchcp 65001 >nul 2>&1\\ntitle Mind Language System\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0\\\"\\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\\n\\n:MENU\\ncls\\necho.\\necho  ===== Mind Language System =====\\necho.\\necho         1. Install + Start (recommended)\\necho         2. Install only\\necho         3. Start bridge only\\necho         4. Package VS Code extension\\necho         5. Usage tutorial\\necho         0. Exit\\necho.\\nset /p choice=\\\"Enter number (0-5): \\\"\\n\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"\\\" goto MENU\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"1\\\" goto INSTALL_AND_START\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"2\\\" goto INSTALL_ONLY\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"3\\\" goto START_ONLY\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"4\\\" goto PACKAGE\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"5\\\" goto TUTORIAL\\nif \\\"%%choice%%\\\"==\\\"0\\\" exit /b\\ngoto MENU\\n\\n:INSTALL_AND_START\\ncls\\necho.\\necho ==== Step 1/5: Check Environment ====\\necho.\\n\\nwhere node >nul 2>&1\\nif %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (\\n    echo [X] Node.js not found^^!\\n    echo     Download from https://nodejs.org/\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\nfor /f \\\"delims=\\\" %%v in ('node --version 2^>nul') do set NODE_VER=%%v\\necho [OK] Node.js: %%NODE_VER%%\\n\\nwhere npm >nul 2>&1\\nif %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (\\n    echo [X] npm not found^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\nfor /f \\\"delims=\\\" %%v in ('npm --version 2^>nul') do set NPM_VER=%%v\\necho [OK] npm: %%NPM_VER%%\\n\\nwhere code >nul 2>&1\\nif %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (\\n    echo [OK] VS Code: installed\\n) else (\\n    echo [!] VS Code CLI not found\\n)\\n\\necho.\\necho ==== Step 2/5: Install Bridge Dependencies ====\\necho.\\n\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\" 2>nul\\nif %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (\\n    echo [X] mind-bridge directory not found^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\nif not exist \\\"package.json\\\" (\\n    echo [X] package.json not found^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\ncall npm install\\nif %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (\\n    echo [X] npm install failed^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\necho [OK] Bridge dependencies installed\\n\\necho.\\necho ==== Step 3/5: Build VS Code Extension ====\\necho.\\n\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" 2>nul\\nif %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (\\n    echo [X] mind-extension directory not found^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\nif not exist \\\"package.json\\\" (\\n    echo [X] package.json not found^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\ncall npm install\\ncall npm run build\\nif %%errorlevel%% neq 0 (\\n    echo [X] Build failed^^!\\n    pause\\n    exit /b\\n)\\necho [OK] Extension built\\n\\necho.\\necho ==== Step 4/5: Start Bridge Service ====\\necho.\\n\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\"\\nstart \\\"Mind Bridge\\\" cmd /c \\\"node src/index.js && pause\\\"\\necho Waiting for service...\\ntimeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul\\n\\ncall :CHECK_HEALTH\\nif %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (\\n    echo [OK] Bridge running on port 3456\\n) else (\\n    echo [!] Bridge may still be starting...\\n    echo     Check http://localhost:3456/health\\n)\\n\\necho.\\necho ==== Step 5/5: Install VS Code Extension ====\\necho.\\necho  Option A -- Install from VSIX^^!:\\necho     cd \\\"%%~dp0mind-extension\\\"\\necho     npx vsce package\\necho     VS Code: Extensions ... Install from VSIX\\necho.\\necho  Option B -- Developer mode:\\necho     Open \\\"%%~dp0mind-extension\\\" in VS Code\\necho     Press F5\\necho.\\necho  ========================================\\necho    All done^^! Create a .mind file to start\\necho  ========================================\\necho.\\npause\\ngoto MENU\\n\\n:INSTALL_ONLY\\ncls\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\" 2>nul && call npm install\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" 2>nul && call npm install && call npm run build\\necho [OK] Done\\npause\\ngoto MENU\\n\\n:START_ONLY\\ncls\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\" 2>nul\\nstart \\\"Mind Bridge\\\" cmd /c \\\"node src/index.js && pause\\\"\\ntimeout /t 5 /nobreak >nul\\ncall :CHECK_HEALTH\\nif %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (\\n    echo [OK] Bridge running on port 3456\\n) else (\\n    echo [!] Bridge may still be starting\\n)\\npause\\ngoto MENU\\n\\n:PACKAGE\\ncls\\ncd /d \\\"%~dp0mind-extension\\\" 2>nul\\ncall npx vsce package\\nif %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (\\n    echo [OK] Extension packaged^^!\\n    dir /b *.vsix 2>nul\\n) else (\\n    echo [!] Package failed\\n)\\npause\\ngoto MENU\\n\\n:TUTORIAL\\ncls\\necho.\\necho  ============ Mind Language System ============\\necho.\\necho  Step 1: Start bridge service\\necho    Run this script -^> option [1]\\necho    Or: cd mind-bridge ^&^& npm start\\necho.\\necho  Step 2: Install VS Code extension\\necho    cd mind-extension ^&^& npx vsce package\\necho    Install .vsix in VS Code\\necho.\\necho  Step 3: Create .mind file\\necho.\\necho  Step 4: Use # @d for code generation\\necho    # @d reverse linked list\\necho    Define function reverse_list\\necho.\\necho  Step 5: Click # @d to jump to code\\necho.\\npause\\ngoto MENU\\n\\n:CHECK_HEALTH\\nwhere curl >nul 2>&1\\nif %%errorlevel%% equ 0 (\\n    curl -s http://localhost:3456/health >nul 2>&1\\n    exit /b %%errorlevel%%\\n)\\npowershell -Command \\\"try { $$r = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri 'http://localhost:3456/health' -TimeoutSec 3; exit 0 } catch { exit 1 }\\\" >nul 2>&1\\nexit /b %%errorlevel%%\\n\\\"@\\n\\n$batContent -replace \\\"`r`n\\\", \\\"`n\\\" | Set-Content -Path \\\"Structured-Pseudocode/package/一键安装启动.bat\\\" -Encoding Default\\nWrite-Host \\\"Written: $($batContent.Length) bytes\\\"\\n\", \"path\": \"/AI   文件夹/write_bat.ps1\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The PowerShell command has issues with the single quotes and the `&&` - the batch file contains `'` characters that conflict with PowerShell's quoting. Let me use a different approach - write the batch file content as a heredoc string with proper escaping.\n\nActually, the simplest fix: write the batch file using a .ps1 script file, or use a different escaping strategy. Let me write a simple PowerShell script that creates the batch file, save it, then run it.\n\nActually, the easiest approach: put the batch content into a separate variable using a here-string, then write it."}
