{"role":"assistant","content":"### 测试 4: start.bat 路径验证\n\n发现一个隐蔽的 bug——`start.bat` 中引用的是 `%~dp0mind-bridge`，但在 git repo 的结构中，`package/start.bat` 的上级是 `extension/` 和 `bridge/`（不是 `mind-bridge/` 和 `mind-extension/`）。","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_P5k3yDeUkxo1kmtVOUdQ8552","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"node -e \\\"\\nconst fs=require('fs');\\nconst old=fs.readFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat','ascii');\\n// Fix: replace %~dp0mind-bridge with %~dp0..\\\\\\\\bridge\\n// and %~dp0mind-extension with %~dp0..\\\\\\\\extension\\nlet fixed=old\\n  .replace(/%~dp0mind-bridge/g,'%~dp0..\\\\\\\\bridge')\\n  .replace(/%~dp0mind-extension/g,'%~dp0..\\\\\\\\extension');\\nfs.writeFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat',Buffer.from(fixed,'ascii'));\\nconsole.log('Fixed. Size:',fixed.length,'bytes');\\n// Also copy to install package\\nrequire('fs').copyFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat','AI   文件夹/Mind-语言系统-安装包/start.bat');\\n// But wait - the install package uses junctions named mind-bridge/mind-extension!\\n// So we need to check if those exist too. Better approach: try both paths.\\nconsole.log('Copied to install package');\\n\\\"\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"All tests pass cleanly. Let me also check for the compile issues with the extension by verifying the build one more time. And let me check the start.bat to make sure it references the right paths.\n\nActually, let me do a dry run of the batch file's logic to check for path issues. The batch file does `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"` and `%~dp0` is the directory of the batch file itself. If the batch file is in `Mind-语言系统-安装包/`, it would look for `Mind-语言系统-安装包/mind-bridge/` which is a junction link.\n\nWait - the batch file in `Structured-Pseudocode/package/` does `cd /d \"%~dp0mind-bridge\"` which resolves to `Structured-Pseudocode/package/mind-bridge/` - but that directory doesn't exist! The git repo doesn't have a mind-bridge folder in the package directory.\n\nThis is a **real bug** - the batch file in the git repo won't work because it references `mind-bridge/` and `mind-extension/` as relative paths, but in the git repo's `package/` directory, those don't exist! They only exist as junctions in the `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` folder.\n\nActually, looking at the git repo structure:\n```\nStructured-Pseudocode/\n├── bridge/          ← source files\n├── extension/       ← source files\n└── package/         ← startup scripts\n    └── start.bat    ← references \"../mind-bridge\" which doesn't exist\n```\n\nThe batch file references `%~dp0mind-bridge` which is `Structured-Pseudocode/package/mind-bridge/` - this doesn't exist!\n\nThe actual locations are:\n- `Structured-Pseudocode/bridge/`\n- `Structured-Pseudocode/extension/`\n\nSo the batch file should reference `%~dp0..\\bridge` and `%~dp0..\\extension`.\n\nAlso the `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` folder has junctions to the actual directories, so the batch file works there but not when copied from the git repo.\n\nLet me fix this. The batch file should reference `..\\bridge` and `..\\extension` relative to its own location in the `package/` directory.\n\nBut wait - the user might run the batch file from different locations:\n1. From `Mind-语言系统-安装包/start.bat` → needs `mind-bridge/` (junction)\n2. From `Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat` → needs `../bridge/`\n\nThe simplest fix is to make the batch file check both relative paths:\n1. First try `%~dp0mind-bridge` (for the junction setup)\n2. If not found, try `%~dp0..\\bridge` (for the git repo structure)\n\nActually, this is getting complicated. The most practical approach is to update the batch file to use `../bridge` and `../extension` paths (relative to the `package/` directory), and the junction-based `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` setup would need a different batch file or the junctions to be structured differently.\n\nAlternatively, I can restructure the `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` to have `bridge/` and `extension/` linking to the source directories:\n\n```\nMind-语言系统-安装包/\n├── start.bat               ← uses current directory\n├── bridge/ ──→ ../mind-bridge  (junction)\n└── extension/ ──→ ../mind-extension  (junction)\n```\n\nBut currently `Mind-语言系统-安装包/` has:\n```\nMind-语言系统-安装包/\n├── start.bat\n├── 使用教程.txt\n├── 示例.mind\n├── mind-bridge/ ──→ ../mind-bridge  (junction)\n└── mind-extension/ ──→ ../mind-extension  (junction)\n```\n\nAnd the batch file references `%~dp0mind-bridge` which works here.\n\nFor the git repo `Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat`, it references `%~dp0mind-bridge` which doesn't exist. The fix is straightforward - update the batch file to first check for `mind-bridge/`, then `../bridge/`, then `../mind-bridge/`.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: just update the batch file to use `../bridge` and `../extension` paths since those are the correct relative paths from the `package/` subdirectory.\n\nLet me update the batch file."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_P5k3yDeUkxo1kmtVOUdQ8552","name":"run_command","content":"$ node -e \"\nconst fs=require('fs');\nconst old=fs.readFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat','ascii');\n// Fix: replace %~dp0mind-bridge with %~dp0..\\\\bridge\n// and %~dp0mind-extension with %~dp0..\\\\extension\nlet fixed=old\n  .replace(/%~dp0mind-bridge/g,'%~dp0..\\\\bridge')\n  .replace(/%~dp0mind-extension/g,'%~dp0..\\\\extension');\nfs.writeFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat',Buffer.from(fixed,'ascii'));\nconsole.log('Fixed. Size:',fixed.length,'bytes');\n// Also copy to install package\nrequire('fs').copyFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat','AI   文件夹/Mind-语言系统-安装包/start.bat');\n// But wait - the install package uses junctions named mind-bridge/mind-extension!\n// So we need to check if those exist too. Better approach: try both paths.\nconsole.log('Copied to install package');\n\"\n[exit 0]\nFixed. Size: 3176 bytes\nCopied to install package\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"路径不统一——安装包用 junction 名 `mind-bridge`，git repo 的目录名是 `bridge`。让 batch 自动检测：","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_5sYILiqxCTIQuMqofPAp7316","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"node -e \\\"\\nconst fs=require('fs');\\n// Read the current fixed version\\nconst content=fs.readFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat','ascii');\\n// We need to change the approach: instead of hardcoded paths,\\n// use a check at the start of each section\\n\\n// The current file has %~dp0..\\\\\\\\bridge and %~dp0..\\\\\\\\extension\\n// Let's add a path detection block at the top\\n\\n// Actually, the cleanest approach: detect at the INSTALL label\\nlet lines=content.split('\\\\r\\\\n');\\nlet result=[];\\n\\nfor(let l of lines){\\n  // Replace the path references with a flexible approach\\n  if(l.includes('cd /d \\\\\\\"%~dp0..\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bridge\\\\\\\"')){\\n    result.push('if exist \\\\\\\"%~dp0mind-bridge\\\\\\\" (');\\n    result.push('  set BRIDGE_DIR=%~dp0mind-bridge');\\n    result.push('  set EXT_DIR=%~dp0mind-extension');\\n    result.push(') else (');\\n    result.push('  set BRIDGE_DIR=%~dp0..\\\\\\\\bridge');\\n    result.push('  set EXT_DIR=%~dp0..\\\\\\\\extension');\\n    result.push(')');\\n    // Also convert subsequent cd commands to use the variable\\n    continue;\\n  }\\n  \\n  // Convert cd commands\\n  l=l.replace(/%~dp0\\\\.\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bridge/g,'%BRIDGE_DIR%');\\n  l=l.replace(/%~dp0\\\\.\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\extension/g,'%EXT_DIR%');\\n  l=l.replace(/%~dp0mind-bridge/g,'%BRIDGE_DIR%');\\n  l=l.replace(/%~dp0mind-extension/g,'%EXT_DIR%');\\n  result.push(l);\\n}\\n\\nconst newContent=result.join('\\\\r\\\\n');\\nfs.writeFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat',Buffer.from(newContent,'ascii'));\\nfs.copyFileSync('Structured-Pseudocode/package/start.bat','AI   文件夹/Mind-语言系统-安装包/start.bat');\\nconsole.log('Done:',newContent.length,'bytes');\\n\\n// Verify key paths\\nc