{"role":"assistant","content":"两个问题分开排查。先看桥接是否在跑：","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_4B8F0PfxT9q4EdPSlOMf1726","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"curl -s --connect-timeout 3 http://localhost:3456/health 2>&1 || echo \\\"DEAD\\\"\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user is reporting two issues:\n\n1. When they type `# @d 你是否能正确工作？` and press Enter, nothing happens (no code generation)\n2. The indentation display is wrong\n\nLet me think about both issues:\n\n### Issue 1: `# @d` not triggering\n\nThe `# @d` detection is in the `codeGenerator.js` bridge file:\n\n```javascript\nexport function hasQueryComments(content) {\n  return content.split('\\n').some(line =>\n    line.trim().startsWith('#') && line.includes('@d')\n  );\n}\n```\n\nAnd in `extension.ts`:\n```typescript\nif (content.includes('@d')) {\n  triggerGeneration(document, config.bridgeHost, config.bridgePort);\n}\n```\n\nLet me check if the bridge is running. If the bridge isn't running, the generation won't work. Also, the `triggerGeneration` function is called inside `triggerAnalysis` which is called on Enter. If the analysis itself fails (because the bridge isn't running or the API is down), then `triggerGeneration` won't be called either.\n\nLet me look at the flow:\n\n```typescript\nasync function triggerAnalysis(document) {\n  // ... sends to analyze endpoint\n  const result = await analyzeContent(content, ...);\n  \n  if (thisVersion !== pendingAnalysisVersion) return; // version mismatch\n  \n  if (result) {\n    // ... apply results ...\n    \n    // ---- 5. 检测 # @d 注释 → 触发代码生成 ----\n    if (content.includes('@d')) {\n      triggerGeneration(document, config.bridgeHost, config.bridgePort);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSo the generation is triggered AFTER analysis succeeds. If analysis fails or times out, generation won't happen.\n\nBut also, the user said \"敲完这一行回车没反应\" - they typed the line and pressed Enter but nothing happened. This could mean:\n1. The bridge isn't running\n2. The analysis is taking too long (20-30 seconds)\n3. The analysis succeeds but generation fails\n\nLet me check if the bridge is running.\n\n### Issue 2: Indentation display is wrong\n\nThe user said \"缩进显示不太对\". Let me check the indentDecoration.ts code. The indentation lines use `├─`, `└─`, and `│` characters. These are Unicode box-drawing characters.\n\nThe issue might be with how I detect indentation and render the lines. Let me look at the `renderIndentLines` function in `indentDecoration.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nfunction parseIndents(document) {\n  for each line:\n    const indentMatch = text.match(/^(\\s*)/);\n    const indentLen = indentMatch ? indentMatch[1].length : 0;\n    result.push({ level: Math.floor(indentLen / 2), ... });\n}\n```\n\nThe issue is that the `level` is calculated as `Math.floor(indentLen / 2)` - meaning every 2 spaces = 1 level. But what if the user uses tabs, or different indentation? \n\nAlso, the `renderIndentLines` function might not be called immediately on Enter because it's called from `triggerAnalysis` -> `applyAnalysisResult`. If the analysis takes 20+ seconds, the indent lines won't appear until the analysis completes.\n\nWait, there's also an `onDidChangeTextDocument` handler in `indentDecoration.ts` that should render indent lines immediately:\n```typescript\nvscode.workspace.onDidChangeTextDocument((event) => {\n  const editor = vscode.window.activeTextEditor;\n  if (editor && editor.document === event.document && editor.document.languageId === 'mind') {\n    renderIndentLines(editor);\n  }\n})\n```\n\nBut wait - the `extension.ts` also has an `onDidChangeTextDocument` handler, and the `indentDecoration.ts` one also fires. But the `indentDecoration.ts` one is more permissive (fires on any text change, not just Enter). So the indent lines should appear immediately on any text change.\n\nUnless the issue is that the indent decorations aren't working at all. Let me think about what \"缩进显示不太对\" means:\n- No indent lines at all?\n- Lines in wrong positions?\n- Wrong branch symbols?\n\nActually, I think the issue might be that the user expects to see indentation lines IMMEDIATELY when they type, not waiting for the AI analysis. The `indentDecoration.ts` has a listener for `onDidChangeTextDocument` that calls `renderIndentLines`, so it should render immediately.\n\nBut wait - I just realized something. The `extension.ts` only triggers analysis on Enter. But `indentDecoration.ts` triggers `renderIndentLines` on EVERY text change (not just Enter). This inconsistency means:\n- Indent lines render on every keystroke (good, immediate)\n- Analysis + generation only on Enter (good, token saving)\n\nBut if the indent lines are wrong, it's a rendering issue. Let me look at the algorithm more carefully.\n\nActually, now I recall - the user mentioned this exact issue earlier in the conversation history! Let me look at the beginning of our conversation:\n\n> @d 你是否能正确工作？我敲完这一行回车没反应，还有那个缩进显示不太对\n\nThis was the very first message in this conversation, where the user was testing the Reasonix chat system, not the Mind plugin. So the user might be testing a completely different thing now.\n\nWait no, this is in the current conversation about the Mind plugin. The user is now testing the plugin they built.\n\nLet me focus on the actual issues:\n\n1. Bridge might not be running - let me check\n2. Indentation display could have bugs\n\nLet me check if the bridge is running first, then investigate the indentation code."}
