{"role":"assistant","content":"Unicode 方块字符（`├─ └─ │`）在当前 VS Code 字体中不显示。换成通用 ASCII 字符：","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_EbeB3lWyeQmzbjXyyLRq9813","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/extension/src/indentDecoration.ts\", \"search\": \"    // ├─ 分支（有后续兄弟）\\n    branchDecos.push(\\n      vscode.window.createTextEditorDecorationType({\\n        before: { contentText: '├─ ', color, fontWeight: 'normal', margin: '0 0 0 0' },\", \"replace\": \"    // |-- 分支（有后续兄弟）\\n    branchDecos.push(\\n      vscode.window.createTextEditorDecorationType({\\n        before: { contentText: '|-- ', color, fontWeight: 'normal', margin: '0 0 0 0' },\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user is showing me that the indent lines display as garbled rectangles/blocks. This is a Unicode font issue - the characters `├─ └─ │` are not being rendered correctly in the user's VS Code editor font.\n\nThe fix options:\n1. Change the indent characters to ASCII alternatives that work with any font (like `|`, `+--`, `\\--`)\n2. Tell the user to install a font that supports these Unicode box-drawing characters\n\nThe simplest fix that will work universally is to replace the Unicode box-drawing characters with ASCII alternatives. Many terminals and editors use these:\n\n- `├─` → `+-`\n- `└─` → `\\-` \n- `│` → `|`\n\nOr better, use the standard ASCII art approach:\n- `├─` → `├─` → `├─` ... no, that's the same issue.\n\nLet me use simpler ASCII characters:\n- `├─ ` → `+-- `\n- `└─ ` → `\\-- `\n- `│ ` → `| `\n\nOr even simpler:\n- Branch: `├── ` → just use `|-- ` \n- Last: `└── ` → use `\\-- `\n- Continuation: `│ ` → `| `\n\nLet me update the indentDecoration.ts to use ASCII characters instead."}
