{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_oRcSv2gMCCRly5eUehFm4858","type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/extension/src/extension.ts\", \"range\": 90-115}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user wants several things:\n\n1. **Bridge health check on every file submission**: When a line is completed (Enter pressed), check if the bridge is healthy before sending the analysis request.\n\n2. **Only analyze on line completion**: Already implemented (only triggered by Enter), but the user wants to emphasize this - no fixed debounce timer, only when a line is finished.\n\n3. **Auto-connect bridge on plugin activation**: When the plugin starts, automatically try to connect the bridge.\n\n4. **Test # @d functionality**: After fixing, test that # @d properly generates code.\n\nLet me look at the current code to see what needs to change.\n\nActually, looking at the current extension.ts:\n\n1. `checkBridgeConnection()` is called in `activate()` - so it already checks on activation ✅\n2. `triggerAnalysis` is only called on Enter - already line-complete based ✅\n3. The health check is already done in `checkBridgeConnection()` ✅\n\nBut the user wants a few more things:\n- \"每次写代码提交文件的时候都检查是否成功\" - Check if bridge is healthy every time before sending\n- \"不要按照固定时间不断提交\" - No fixed debounce timer\n- \"写好了之后测试是否能正确的利用#@d来正确回答\" - Test # @d after fixing\n\nLet me look at `triggerAnalysis` to see if we should add a health check before sending the request:\n\nCurrently:\n```typescript\nasync function triggerAnalysis(document: vscode.TextDocument): Promise<void> {\n  // ... checks content, cache ...\n  \n  const result = await analyzeContent(content, config.bridgeHost, config.bridgePort);\n  \n  // ... process result ...\n  \n  if (content.includes('@d')) {\n    triggerGeneration(document, config.bridgeHost, config.bridgePort);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nI should add:\n1. A health check before calling `analyzeContent`\n2. Better status display showing bridge connection state\n\nFor the \"写完一行才桥接提交修改\" - this is already implemented (only Enter triggers analysis). But let me double-check by reading the relevant code.\n\nLet me also look at the debounce mechanism - the current code has `LINE_COMPLETE_DELAY = 200` which is a short 200ms delay after Enter. The user doesn't want \"固定时间不断提交\" which I interpret as they don't want a polling mechanism or a timer-based approach. The 200ms delay after Enter is just to let the editor settle, not a periodic timer.\n\nLet me make these improvements clear and test the # @d flow."}
