d-extension\\%VSIX%` when `%~dp0` is `C:\\Users\\27063\\Desktop\\工具箱\\AI   文件夹\\Mind-语言系统-安装包\\`, the `..` goes to `C:\\Users\\27063\\Desktop\\工具箱\\AI   文件夹\\`, then `mind-extension\\mind-language-1.0.0.vsix`. That file exists!\n\nBut the batch file says \"Cannot find\". Let me think about what could go wrong...\n\nActually, looking at the error message more carefully:\n```\n================================\n  Mind ��  echo ================================\n\n[X] Cannot find mind-language-1.0.0.vsix\n```\n\nThe garbled text `Mind ��  echo` suggests the batch file's encoding is causing issues. The `echo =====` line seems to have gotten mangled, which means the file has encoding problems.\n\nWait, looking at the error output:\n```\n================================\n  Mind ��  echo ================================\n```\n\nThis looks like two echo lines got merged: `echo ===== Mind` and another `echo =====` got mangled together. This might be a CRLF issue again.\n\nActually, looking at the original batch file code:\n```\necho ================================\necho   Mind 插件 — 一键更新\necho ================================\n```\n\nThe \"—\" (em dash) might be causing the encoding issue on some terminal configurations. But the bigger issue is that it entered the `FOR` loop condition and printed the error message.\n\nLet me think about why the path detection fails. Let me trace through the logic:\n\n```\nset VSIX=mind-language-1.0.0.vsix\nif exist \"%~dp0..\\extension\\%VSIX%\" (\n  set VSIX_PATH=%~dp0..\\extension\\%VSIX%\n) else if exist \"%~dp0..\\mind-extension\\%VSIX%\" (\n  set VSIX_PATH=%~dp0..\\mind-extension\\%VSIX%\n) else if exist \"%VSIX%\" (\n  set VSIX_PATH=%VSIX%\n) else (\n  echo [X] Cannot find %VSIX%\n  pause\n  exit /b\n)\n```\n\nIf the batch file is running from `Structured-Pseudocode\\package\\`:\n1. `%~dp0..\\extension\\%VSIX%` → `Structured-Pseudocode\\extension\\mind-language-1.0.0.vsix` — doesn't exist!\n2. `%~dp0..\\mind-extension\\%VSIX%` → `Structured-Pseudocode\\mind-extension\\mind-language-1.0.0.vsix` — doesn't exist!\n3. `%VSIX%` → `mind-language-1.0.0.vsix` — doesn't exist in current dir!\n\nAll three fail → \"Cannot find\"\n\nThe fix: add another path check for `..\\..\\extension\\%VSIX%` or check the user's Desktop Toolbox path.\n\nActually, the simplest fix: the .vsix is generated in `AI   文件夹\\mind-extension\\` directory. The batch file should also look there directly."}
