{"role":"assistant","content":"### 1. 添加 3 秒自动重连","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_0sgelHvKrgnQUeKHcIKf2459","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/extension/src/extension.ts\", \"search\": \"  console.log('[Mind] 插件激活完成');\", \"replace\": \"  // ---- 9. 每 3 秒检查桥接状态，断开时自动重连 ----\\n  const healthTimer = setInterval(() => {\\n    if (!bridgeConnected) {\\n      console.log('[Mind] 尝试重连桥接...');\\n      checkBridgeConnection();\\n    }\\n  }, 3000);\\n  context.subscriptions.push({ dispose: () => clearInterval(healthTimer) });\\n\\n  console.log('[Mind] 插件激活完成');\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Now I understand the session manager. It tracks sessions but doesn't actually provide any \"context continuity\" - it's basically just logging.\n\nFor the user's request:\n1. **Auto-reconnect every 3 seconds** - Add a `setInterval` in `activate()`\n2. **Session continuity** - I need to actually track analysis history per file and pass it to the bridge as context\n\nBut for #2, the bridge is stateless. To implement true session continuity, I would need to:\n- Store the full history of previous file contents and analysis results per file\n- Include the previous file content + previous analysis as context in the next request\n\nThis would make the DeepSeek analysis more contextually aware. Let me implement both changes.\n\nLet me make the changes:\n1. Add auto-reconnect interval in extension.ts\n2. In sessionManager.ts, add storage of previous analysis context\n3. In bridgeClient.ts, optionally send previous context with the request\n4. In the bridge, accept and use the previous context\n\nActually, for simplicity, let me just:\n1. Add the auto-reconnect\n2. Store previous analysis results in sessionManager\n3. Pass previous content + analysis as context in the next request\n\nFor the bridge, I need to update mindAnalyzer.js to accept optional `previousContent` and `previousResult` parameters and include them in the prompt for continuity.\n\nThis is getting complex. Let me do the simplest meaningful implementation:\n1. Auto-reconnect timer\n2. Store the last analysis result per file in sessionManager\n3. The existing behavior already sends the full file each time, which IS the context continuity\n\nActually, the user's original request was about Reasonix creating corresponding sessions. The mind-bridge IS the \"Reasonix\" for this plugin. Each request to the bridge already sends the full file. The key issue is that the bridge doesn't remember past requests.\n\nLet me implement:\n1. Add 3-second health check interval\n2. Store previous file content + analysis in sessionManager\n3. Pass previous analysis as context in the next /analyze request\n4. Update the bridge to use this context"}
