{"role":"assistant","content":"我理解你的意思了——你希望每个 `.mind` 文件的分析对话，都能在 reasonix CLI 里看到并能切进去继续说。\n\n目前桥接是无状态的，每次分析都是独立请求。要实现\"能切进去接着说\"，需要做两件事：\n\n1. **桥接保存每份文件的完整对话记录（transcript）** → 可查看\n2. **对话模式** → 不只是分析文件，能接收追问\n\n先看看当前 `reasonix` CLI 的能力：","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_MwNz14axUSyLLufdLpNR4567","type":"function","function":{"name":"run_command","arguments":"{\"command\": \"reasonix --help 2>&1 | findstr \\\"session transcript replay\\\"\"}"}}],"reasoning_content":"The user wants to see the conversation sessions in the Reasonix terminal and be able to switch into them to continue the conversation. \n\nThis is a significant feature request. The user wants:\n1. Each `.mind` file's analysis history to be visible in the Reasonix terminal\n2. The ability to jump into a conversation from the terminal\n\nBut I need to think about what \"Reasonix\" means here. Reasonix is me - the AI assistant running in this environment. The user wants to see the `.mind` analysis conversations in my interface.\n\nWait - the user has the `reasonix` CLI tool installed globally (version 0.48.0). They run it in their terminal. So \"reasonix 终端\" means when they run `reasonix` in their terminal, they want to see the `.mind` analysis sessions there and continue the conversation.\n\nThis is quite complex. Reasonix (the CLI tool) has its own session management and wouldn't automatically know about the mind-bridge's sessions.\n\nHowever, there's a simpler interpretation: the user wants the mind-bridge to log sessions in a way that's visible to them, and they want to be able to continue the conversation through the bridge.\n\nLet me think about what's practical:\n\n1. **Log sessions to files**: Save each `.mind` file's analysis conversation as a JSONL transcript that can be viewed\n2. **Continue conversation**: Allow sending follow-up messages (not just file analysis) to the bridge\n\nActually, the simplest approach that addresses the user's request:\n1. Save the conversation history (all exchanges) per `.mind` file to a visible location\n2. Allow the user to add free-form comments/questions to the `.mind` file (like `# @d question`) that get analyzed as part of the conversation\n\nBut I think what the user really wants is:\n1. When they're in the Reasonix terminal, they want to see what the `.mind` plugin has been discussing\n2. They want to be able to say \"continue this\" from the terminal\n\nThis would require the mind-bridge to either:\n- Save transcripts to a shared location that Reasonix reads\n- Or have an API that Reasonix can query\n\nThe most practical approach:\n1. The mind-bridge saves per-file conversation transcripts as JSONL files in a visible directory\n2. The user can view these transcripts with the `reasonix` CLI tool\n\nLet me implement transcript saving in the mind-bridge and update the plugin to include conversation context properly."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_00_MwNz14axUSyLLufdLpNR4567","name":"run_command","content":"$ reasonix --help 2>&1 | findstr \"session transcript replay\"\n[exit 0]\n  stats [transcript]             显示使用情况仪表板。\n  sessions [options] [name]      列出保存的聊天会话，或按名称检查。\n  prune-sessions [options]       删除空闲 ≥N 天的已保存会话（默认 90）。使用 --dry-run 预览。\n  replay [options] <transcript>  交互式 Ink TUI，用于浏览转录稿。\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"`reasonix sessions` 和 `reasonix replay` 可以查看和回放对话。我来把 `.mind` 的分析对话转成 reasonix 兼容的转录文件，这样你就能用 `reasonix replay` 回看，并能切进去继续说。","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_00_PlqiiotqDS30S7Fu0lMp9586","type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Structured-Pseudocode/bridge/src/index.js\", \"range\": 1-10}"}}],"reasoning_content":"Reasonix CLI has:\n- `sessions` - list saved chat sessions\n- `replay <transcript>` - browse a transcript interactively\n\nThis is for Reasonix's own chat sessions, not for mind-bridge data. But what I can do is:\n\n1. **Save transcripts in Reasonix-compatible format**: The bridge can save analysis conversations as JSONL files that Reasonix can replay with `reasonix replay`\n2. **Create a way to \"continue\"**: When the user is in Reasonix terminal and wants to continue a .mind conversation, they can run something like `reasonix run --transcript path/to/session.jsonl \"继续分析这个文件\"`\n\nBut this is limited. Let me think about what's actually useful:\n\nThe simplest approach that gives the user what they want:\n1. The bridge saves each `.mind` file's analysis history as a JSONL transcript in `~/.reasonix/transcripts/` or similar\n2. The user can do `reasonix replay <path>` to see the full conversation\n3. When they want to continue, they can add `# @d 追问...` to the `.mind` file\n\nActually, I think the most practical approach is to make the mind-bridge save transcripts in a format that Reasonix can work with. Let me implement:\n\n1. Bridge saves per-file conversation transcripts as JSONL files\n2. Files are saved to `~/.reasonix/mind-transcripts/`\n3. The user can run `reasonix replay <path>` to view them\n\nLet me add transcript saving to the mind-bridge."}
